@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080
@alertId = 3830c273-0c57-40bd-8bc4-a6d339d10211
@workOrderId = replace-with-workOrderId-from-response
@vendorError = false
@dbUpdateError = false
@dbCommitError = false

### Creates a new work order on every invocation, even with the same alertId.
POST {{baseUrl}}/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "alertId": "{{alertId}}",
  "busId": "B-42",
  "timestamp": "2026-01-15T08:30:00Z",
  "odometerKm": 182340.5,
  "engineTempC": 115,
  "brakePadThicknessMm": 3.2,
  "faultCodes": ["P0217"],
  "vendorError": {{vendorError}},
  "dbUpdateError": {{dbUpdateError}},
  "dbCommitError": {{dbCommitError}}
}

### Set vendorError above to true to request httpbin's HTTP 503 endpoint.
### The service returns 502, but the work order stays saved.
### dbUpdateError simulates a failed write (500, no row inserted).
### dbCommitError is ignored: this demo has no explicit transaction.

### Inspect the saved work order, including after a failed vendor POST.
GET {{baseUrl}}/work-orders/{{workOrderId}}

### Missing work order: 404.
GET {{baseUrl}}/work-orders/missing

### Missing required telemetry fields: 400, no writes.
POST {{baseUrl}}/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### OpenAPI contract.
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json

### Local service health (not vendor availability).
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
